hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23870","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Mujahid who said: I entered, I and Yahya ibn Ja'dah, upon a man of the Ansar among the companions of the Messenger, he said: They mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a freedwoman of Banu Abdilmuttalib, and said: She stands the night and fasts the day, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But I sleep and pray, and fast and break fast, so whoever follows me is of me, and whoever turns away from my sunnah is not of me, every deed has eagerness, then slackness, so whoever's slackness is toward innovation has strayed, and whoever's slackness is toward sunnah has been guided."
"23871","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Abdurrahman ibn Salamah al-Khuza'i from his uncle who said: We came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Ashura, and we had eaten lunch, so he said: Did you fast this day, he said: We said: We have eaten lunch, he said: So complete the rest of your day."
"23872","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Hasna bint Mu'awiyah of Banu Suraym who said: My uncle narrated to us, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is in Paradise, he said: The Prophet is in Paradise, and the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn and the infant girl."
